<p>Harvest represents the changing face of North Alabama — a community that's grown dramatically over the past two decades and continues to expand. New subdivisions spring up regularly, attracting families who want space and value without being far from Huntsville's employment centers.</p>

<p>This growth creates two distinct gutter challenges. Newer homes typically have builder-grade gutters — the cheapest option that technically meets code. Thin materials, seams every 10 feet, often undersized for our rainfall. These systems start failing within 5-10 years. Meanwhile, Harvest's established properties have older gutter systems that have reached the end of their lifespan, plus mature trees that constantly fill gutters with debris.</p>

<p>Whether your home is brand new or has been here for decades, your gutters need to handle North Alabama's 55+ inches of annual rainfall and the region's intense storms. That's what Blue River Gutters provides.</p>
